    "verdict": "JSONL. A whole-disc filter is 10 ms with grep and needs no reader; a full parse of every row is 0.33 s, which is below the noise floor of any consumer that was spending 15 to 953 s walking. SQLite's indexed query is ~800x faster than the full parse and saves 0.33 s on a 15 s task, in exchange for a binary artefact git cannot diff and grep cannot read. A consumer that ever needs indexed queries builds the database from the JSONL in 0.53 s."
